    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Question\n\nI just saw that in neovim 0.12 the `nvim_open_win()` is now populated with statusline and I assume we use that (haven't look the code yet) and I have this:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"646\" height=\"201\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be2406f2-5f05-4027-b3fb-ee6b9626a7f8\" />\r\n\r\nmy statusline is inside mini.files.\r\n\r\nbut this is a customized one that I made myself and these are my status line config (and I use `opt_local` if this does make a difference):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal branch = vim.fn.system 'git branch --show-current 2>/dev/null | tr -d \"\\n\"'\r\nlocal branch_status = function()\r\n  if branch ~= '' then\r\n    return '[' .. branch .. ']'\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  return ''\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal get_time = function()\r\n  local get_time_string = os.date '%H:%M'\r\n\r\n  return '[' .. get_time_string .. ']'\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinEnter', 'BufEnter' }, {\r\n  callback = function()\r\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\r\n      '%#StatusLine#',\r\n      branch_status(),\r\n      '%y',\r\n      '%=',\r\n      '[%f]',\r\n      '%=',\r\n      '%h%w%m%r[%l:%c][%P]',\r\n      get_time(),\r\n    }\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinLeave', 'BufLeave' }, {\r\n  callback = function()\r\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\r\n      '%#StatusLineNC#',\r\n      '[%f]',\r\n    }\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\na rather simple one I reckon, and I also use `Win*` groups for this...\r\n\r\ndo this make a difference? since this hasn't happened when I haven't updated yet to nvim 0.12 and the recent mini.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.files</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I just saw that in neovim 0.12 the <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim_open_win()</code> is now populated with statusline and I assume we use that (haven't look the code yet) and I have this:</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1876018/573598770-be2406f2-5f05-4027-b3fb-ee6b9626a7f8.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..y9Lp3nN-sfdQotDkQJ360Bglm099pXviS-IAdZQIWRg\"><img width=\"646\" height=\"201\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1876018/573598770-be2406f2-5f05-4027-b3fb-ee6b9626a7f8.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..y9Lp3nN-sfdQotDkQJ360Bglm099pXviS-IAdZQIWRg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 201px;; aspect-ratio: 646 / 201; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">my statusline is inside mini.files.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">but this is a customized one that I made myself and these are my status line config (and I use <code class=\"notranslate\">opt_local</code> if this does make a difference):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local branch = vim.fn.system 'git branch --show-current 2&gt;/dev/null | tr -d &quot;\\n&quot;'\nlocal branch_status = function()\n  if branch ~= '' then\n    return '[' .. branch .. ']'\n  end\n\n  return ''\nend\n\nlocal get_time = function()\n  local get_time_string = os.date '%H:%M'\n\n  return '[' .. get_time_string .. ']'\nend\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinEnter', 'BufEnter' }, {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\n      '%#StatusLine#',\n      branch_status(),\n      '%y',\n      '%=',\n      '[%f]',\n      '%=',\n      '%h%w%m%r[%l:%c][%P]',\n      get_time(),\n    }\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinLeave', 'BufLeave' }, {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\n      '%#StatusLineNC#',\n      '[%f]',\n    }\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">branch</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">system</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>git branch --show-current 2&gt;/dev/null | tr -d \"<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>\"<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">branch_status</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">branch</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">branch</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">get_time</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">get_time_string</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">os.date</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%H:%M<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">get_time_string</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>WinEnter<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>BufEnter<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}, {\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt_local</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">statusline</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.concat</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%#StatusLine#<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-c1\">branch_status</span>(),\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%y<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%=<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[%f]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%=<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%h%w%m%r[%l:%c][%P]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-c1\">get_time</span>(),\n    }\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>WinLeave<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>BufLeave<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}, {\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt_local</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">statusline</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.concat</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%#StatusLineNC#<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>[%f]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n    }\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">a rather simple one I reckon, and I also use <code class=\"notranslate\">Win*</code> groups for this...</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">do this make a difference? since this hasn't happened when I haven't updated yet to nvim 0.12 and the recent mini.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.files\nQuestion\nI just saw that in neovim 0.12 the nvim_open_win() is now populated with statusline and I assume we use that (haven't look the code yet) and I have this:\n\nmy statusline is inside mini.files.\nbut this is a customized one that I made myself and these are my status line config (and I use opt_local if this does make a difference):\nlocal branch = vim.fn.system 'git branch --show-current 2>/dev/null | tr -d \"\\n\"'\nlocal branch_status = function()\n  if branch ~= '' then\n    return '[' .. branch .. ']'\n  end\n\n  return ''\nend\n\nlocal get_time = function()\n  local get_time_string = os.date '%H:%M'\n\n  return '[' .. get_time_string .. ']'\nend\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinEnter', 'BufEnter' }, {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\n      '%#StatusLine#',\n      branch_status(),\n      '%y',\n      '%=',\n      '[%f]',\n      '%=',\n      '%h%w%m%r[%l:%c][%P]',\n      get_time(),\n    }\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinLeave', 'BufLeave' }, {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.opt_local.statusline = table.concat {\n      '%#StatusLineNC#',\n      '[%f]',\n    }\n  end,\n})\na rather simple one I reckon, and I also use Win* groups for this...\ndo this make a difference? since this hasn't happened when I haven't updated yet to nvim 0.12 and the recent mini.",
